JJ1 = ("我父母原来都是中国人，他们很重视我的教育，为了给我一个好的学习环境，在我很小的时候，就带我移民到美国。我是在美国长大的，为了我有一个美好的未来，父母做什么都愿意。", "My parents were originally both Chinese. They attached great importance to my education, and in order to give me a good learning environment they took me to immigrate to the U.S. when I was very little. I grew up in America, and for me to have a bright future my parents were willing to do anything. (translations of Jingjing’s story are mine)")
JJ2 = ("来美国五年左右，父母就在离我家不远的地方，买了一座农舍。那座农舍不大，也很破旧，但前后院却很大。在以后的差不多七、八年的时间里，每个周末，爸爸妈妈都要带上我，开车去那里翻修那座破旧的房子。一到那里，他们就忙着干活儿，我呢，就在前后院子里跑来跑去。跑累了，我就坐在车里看书。那时我在上中学，年龄还小，从来没想到过问他们：“为什么周末你们不休息，要走那么远，干那么累的活儿呢？”", "About five years after we came to America, my parents bought a farmhouse not far from our home. The farmhouse was not big and was very run-down, but the front and back yards were large. For the next seven or eight years, every weekend Mom and Dad would take me and drive there to renovate the dilapidated house. As soon as they arrived they were busy working, while I ran around in the front and back yards. When I was tired of running I sat in the car and read. At that time I was in middle school and still young, and it never occurred to me to ask them: “Why don’t you rest on weekends, and go so far and do such tiring work?”")
JJ3 = ("后来，我上了大学，我的学习成绩一直很好，所以，毕业后，我想先去哈佛大学或斯坦福大学读一个ＭＢＡ，然后到华尔街工作。我和父母说了自己的想法以后，他们非常高兴，鼓励我说：“好，我们支持你！”可是，去那样的学校读书，不但学费很贵，生活费也不便宜，每年最少也要十万美元以上。让我去上那么贵的学校，他们哪来那么多钱哪？", "Later I went to university, and my grades were always very good, so after graduating I wanted to go first to Harvard or Stanford for an MBA and then work on Wall Street. After I told my parents my idea they were very happy and encouraged me: “Good, we support you!” But going to such a school, not only is the tuition very expensive, living expenses are not cheap either, at least 100,000 U.S. dollars or more a year. To let me attend such an expensive school, where would they get so much money? (the book writes MBA in Latin letters and 10 万 in digits)")
JJE = ("爸爸好像看出了我的心思，马上对我说，“钱的事儿你不用担心，钱我们会为你准备好。”原来，他和妈妈早就计划好，等我上学需要钱的时候，他们就把现在住的房子卖掉，搬到那座农舍去。我呢，就可以用卖房子的钱，去最好的学校读ＭＢＡ了。我从心里感谢他们，我要更努力学习，工作，将来能让他们过上一个幸福的晚年。", "Dad seemed to see through my thoughts and immediately said to me, “You don’t need to worry about money; we will have the money ready for you.” It turned out that he and Mom had long ago planned that when I needed money for school they would sell the house they live in now and move to that farmhouse. And I could use the money from selling the house to go to the best school for an MBA. I thank them from my heart; I will study and work even harder so that in the future I can let them live a happy old age. (the original ending, with my translation)")
JJK = [("她的父母很重视她的教育。为了给她一个好的学习环境，在她很小的时候就带她移民到美国。", "Activity 3B-1 (my answer): Her parents valued her education; to give her a good learning environment they took her to immigrate to the U.S. when she was very little."), ("她父母买了农舍以后，每个周末都带她去翻修那座破旧的房子。她当时年纪小，没想到问父母为什么这么累。", "3B-2 (my answer; the book’s 2008 appears in the printed question): After buying the farmhouse her parents took her every weekend to renovate the dilapidated house. She was young then and didn’t think of asking why they worked so hard."),
       ("学费和生活费可能是父母把现在住的房子卖掉的钱。", "3B-3 (my answer): The tuition and living expenses might come from the money from selling the house her parents live in now. (the book’s question mentions Harvard and Stanford)"),
       ("爸爸好像看出了我的心思，马上对我说，“钱的事儿你不用担心，因为我们早就为你准备好了。你好好学习就行。”", "The ending (my own version, finishing the book’s opening line): Dad seemed to see through my thoughts and immediately said to me, “You don’t need to worry about money, because we prepared it for you long ago. Just study well.”")]
L3 = lesson(
    "Lesson 28 Presentation 1 using Chinese in context: Jingjing and her parents’ farmhouse, and vocabulary",
    "靖靖 · 移民 · 农舍 · 翻修 · 哈佛 斯坦福 · 学费 生活费 · 总是 · 子女 · 舍得 · 前途 · 目标",
    requires=[],
    cards=[
        card("Using Chinese in Context, Activity 3 (Reading, Speaking, and Writing)",
             "A. Jingjing is Chinese American, and she is your friend’s friend. Read her story below. B. Work with a classmate to answer the following questions, then individually write the ending. The beginning sentences have been provided: 1. 她的父母重视她的教育吗？ 2. 2008 年她父母买农舍以后，又做什么了？她当时是怎么想的？ 3. 如果哈佛大学或斯坦福大学录取她的话，你觉得她的学费和生活费会从哪儿来？ The ending: 爸爸好像看出了我的心思，马上对我说，“钱的事儿你不用担心，…… C. Discuss your work with your partner. D. Below is the ending of the original article. Discuss what the parents did for their daughter, and then translate it into English. E. Prepare a story of your own about educating children in a U.S. family. Share your work with the class. The story (in three parts), the original ending and my answers:",
             examples=[D(*JJ1), D(*JJ2), D(*JJ3), D(*JJE)] + [D(z, e) for z, e in JJK]),
    ],
    exercises=[
        M("Why did Jingjing’s parents take her to the U.S.?", "To give her a good learning environment", ["To find a job", "To visit family", "To go on vacation"], "为了给我一个好的学习环境."),
        M("What did her parents buy about five years after coming to America?", "A farmhouse", ["A restaurant", "A car", "A school"], "买了一座农舍."),
        M("What was the farmhouse like?", "Small and run-down but with large yards", ["Big and new", "Tiny with no yard", "Beautiful and expensive"], "不大，也很破旧，但前后院却很大."),
        M("What did Jingjing do while her parents worked?", "Ran around the yards and read in the car", ["Worked with them", "Slept all day", "Painted the walls"], "跑来跑去…坐在车里看书."),
        M("What did she want to do after graduating from university?", "Study for an MBA and work on Wall Street", ["Become a teacher", "Go back to China", "Open a restaurant"], "读一个MBA，然后到华尔街工作."),
        M("How much did a year at such a school cost, at least?", "100,000 U.S. dollars or more", ["1,000 dollars", "10,000 yuan", "Nothing"], "每年最少也要十万美元以上."),
        M("What had her parents planned long ago?", "To sell their house and move to the farmhouse", ["To borrow from a friend", "To move back to China", "To sell the farmhouse"], "把现在住的房子卖掉，搬到那座农舍去."),
        M("What does Jingjing want for her parents in the future?", "A happy old age", ["A bigger house", "A new car", "A trip abroad"], "幸福的晚年."),
        F("爸爸好像看出了我的心___。", "思", PART, "心思: thoughts."),
        F("他们哪来那么多钱___？", "哪", ["吗", "了", "过"], "哪: sentence-final particle."),
    ],
)

